<Base title="About — Ifeyi Batindek">
  <section class="wrap-prose">
    <header class="page-head">
      <h1>About</h1>
      <p class="subtitle">Architect, writer, and a few other things, in that order.</p>
    </header>

    <article class="prose">
      <p>I am Ifeyi Batindek. I live and work in Yaoundé, Cameroon. I lead the modernization of the core banking platform at <a href="https://www.creditfoncier.cm/" rel="noopener">Crédit Foncier du Cameroun</a>, a national institution — moving a forty-year-old system to one capable of carrying the next thirty.</p>

      <p>The technical work is demanding. The structural questions are harder. Who decides what the system optimizes for? Whose definitions of risk, eligibility, and trust get encoded into the new architecture? Which dependencies are we quietly accepting in exchange for capability? These are the architecture questions I find most interesting, and the ones I want to spend the next phase of my career on.</p>

      <h2>What I do</h2>
      <p>I design and ship banking-grade software systems: core banking modernization, microservices and event-driven architecture, real-time data pipelines (Kafka, Debezium, CDC), API design, and the operational discipline (Kubernetes, CI/CD, observability) that makes modern software possible to actually run in regulated environments.</p>

      <p>Increasingly, I work on the layer above — bringing AI into systems where the cost of getting it wrong is asymmetric. I've built and published a small open-source <a href="https://github.com/ifeyi/banking-rag-prototype" rel="noopener">RAG prototype for banking documentation</a>, and I write about AI governance and digital sovereignty as architectural concerns rather than abstractions.</p>

      <h2>Background</h2>
      <p>Lead Developer & Enterprise Architect at Crédit Foncier du Cameroun (2024 — present). Before that: Senior Full-Stack Developer & Tech Lead at ST Digital (2022 — 2024) and Software Engineer & Information Systems Manager at CICC (2016 — 2022).</p>

      <p>MBA in Organization Management from ESSEC Business School Douala (2019 — 2021). Bachelor's in Software Engineering from IUT Douala (2009 — 2012). Working toward AWS Certified AI Practitioner, TOGAF, PRINCE2 and PMP in 2026.</p>

      <h2>Working with me</h2>
      <p>I am internationally mobile and currently looking for senior architecture roles — preferably in regulated industries (banking, public sector, healthcare) or in environments where infrastructure scarcity, regulatory constraint, or bilingual operating context is part of the work rather than an afterthought. French (native), English (professional). Open to roles in Europe or fully remote.</p>

      <p>For project enquiries, talks, or correspondence: <a href="mailto:ifeyibatindek@gmail.com">ifeyibatindek@gmail.com</a>. For code and prototypes: <a href="https://github.com/ifeyi" rel="noopener">github.com/ifeyi</a>.</p>

      <hr />

      <p style="font-size: 0.95rem; color: var(--grey-mid);">This site is built with Astro, written by hand, and intentionally small. The colophon has the details.</p>
    </article>
